Here is one of my more interesting deaths.  As a 5th level Archealogist, and
having recently learned in a previous game that were-creatures count as human
when it comes to sacrifices, I found myself in a bas situation.  I had just
been bit by a were-jackal.  After killing him off, I turned into a jackal. My
status with my god wasn't very good, since I had recently prayed to him for
help.  But I wanted to be rid of this lycanthropy! Now! So, I sacrificed the
were-jackal I'd killed earlier at my altar, figuring that it wouldn't be so
bad for me if I were still a jackal myself, ie. not human.  Bad news! 
Blood spills over the altar, and God says, "Thou shallt die!" and sends me
Yeenoghu to play with. Gulp! I'm inside Yeenogu. Stab! Ouch! I'm sick, and
hurting. Stab! Ouch! I'm almost dead! Should I pray? Why not? So, while
sick and dying inside Yeenoghu, I am struck down by lightening from God!
Wonder how much bad Karma one gets for that?


